@startuml Load Sign-off and Declarations Process

title Process: signing off a vehicle's load and declaring it
caption Target design. Decisions P6, X3, X6, X5, D4, D12, D20, X1, O32, D34. Plan 08.

|Dispatcher|
start
:Allocate attested boxes to the vehicle;
:Propose the manifest;

|Administrator|
if (Approve the load?) then (no)
  :Reject;
  |Dispatcher|
  :Fix the load and propose again;
  stop
else (yes)
  |Administrator|
  :Approve (sign-off only, nothing is filed);
endif

|Dispatcher|
:Mark the vehicle's declarations ready to file;
|Freedom|
:Store a snapshot of the load;

|Dispatcher|
fork
  :Take the ENS filing sheet (no address);
  :File the ENS in the EU portal;
  |Ground Officer|
  :Enter the consignee address in the portal;
  |Dispatcher|
  :Record the MRN;
  if (ELO mode automatic?) then (yes)
    :File the ELO in Freedom;
    |Freedom|
    :Enqueue the envelope request;
    |Customs Worker|
    :Create the envelope with French customs;
  else (no, default)
    |Dispatcher|
    :Request the envelope by hand;
    :Record its reference;
  endif
fork again
  |Dispatcher|
  if (GMR mode automatic?) then (yes)
    :File the GMR in Freedom;
    |Customs Worker|
    :Create the GMR with HMRC;
  else (no, default)
    |Dispatcher|
    :Create the GMR in the HMRC portal;
    :Record its reference;
  endif
fork again
  |Dispatcher|
  :Prepare a goods list per Receiver;
  :Send it to the Receiver;
  |Receiver|
  :File it in Ukraine's humanitarian aid system;
  :Return the unique code;
  |Dispatcher|
  :Record the goods-list reference;
end fork

|Freedom|
:Warn the Dispatcher a week before a code or declaration expires;
stop

@enduml
